```

We should also make sure that SSE2 support is not assumed as it's not a given on ix86. Our buildsystem has SSE2 support and compiles binary for it, but for example on my Linux distro the i586 is without SSE2 so the generated binaries have greater compability (it's arguable whether using Embree without SSE2 on a Pentium III is really worth the pain, but well ;)).

The crash reported by @qarmin seems to come from the fact that `Lightmapper` is not being picked by the doctool,while `LightmapperCPU` is. 

@akien-mga I'm not sure what's the policy on these editor-only and internal classes, should I just remove the `register_class` call from the `lightmapper_cpu` module?

I included it because I copied the module from master's `lightmapper_rd`, but removing it fixes the issue while keeping the functionality. Also, I wasn't planning on documenting the class anyways because its usage is only internal.

